---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import UsageCard from '../components/UsageCard.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import { groups, arp, usb } from '../data/usage.js';
import { LED } from '../lib/drawing.js';
import '../styles/site.css';

// CI copies the firmware into public/ and passes its commit and date
const sha = process.env.FIRMWARE_SHA ?? 'dev';
const date = process.env.FIRMWARE_DATE ?? '';
const file = `CHOMPI_MIXTAPE_${sha}.bin`;
const kb = fs.existsSync(`public/${file}`) ? Math.round(fs.statSync(`public/${file}`).size / 1024) : 0;
// the side menu: each section and its cards
const nav = [...groups.map(({ title, cards }) => ({ title, id: `${title}-head`, cards })),
  { title: 'Arpeggiator', id: 'arp-head', cards: arp }, { title: 'USB', id: 'usb-head', cards: usb }];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>MIXTAPE</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400..800&family=Rubik:wght@400;500;700&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap">
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="top">
      <div>
        <h1 aria-label="MIXTAPE">{[...'MIXTAPE'].map((ch) => <span>{ch}</span>)}</h1>
        <p class="sub">TAPE 2.0 for CHOMPI, with a few features I found useful.</p>
        <a class="download" href={file} download>Download firmware</a>
        <a class="ghost" href="tutorial/">Tutorial</a>
        <p class="facts">{kb} KB, built {date}<br><a href="https://github.com/lost-tty/CHOMPI">Source</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero"><Panel leds={{ wheel_l: LED.blue, wheel_r: LED.blue, loop: LED.magenta, line: LED.pink }} /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="block features">
      <h2>Features</h2>
      <div class="overview">
        <div>
          <h3>Looper</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#length">Double or halve the loop length</a></li>
            <li><a href="#step">Step through the sections of a halved loop</a></li>
            <li><a href="#loopedit">Cut the loop by hand with START and END</a></li>
            <li><a href="#undo">Undo and redo the last overdub or FX bake</a></li>
            <li><a href="#bake">Bake the FX into the loop</a></li>
            <li><a href="#copy">Queue a saved loop to start at the end of the current pass, or append it</a></li>
            <li><a href="#tempo">Snap the first loop and playback to the beat, from MIDI clock or the metronome</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Sampling</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#threshold">Recording threshold: sampling starts when the input gets loud enough</a></li>
            <li><a href="#mono">Mono line in: a mono cable plays on both channels</a></li>
            <li><a href="#trim">Trim a sample, and hear the point and the seam</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Keys</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#legato">Legato and glide, saved per slot</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Effects</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#delay">Delay syncs to the beat once the metronome or MIDI clock is on</a></li>
            <li><a href="#grains">Grains past full reverb, hold the knob to freeze</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Drum kits</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#kits">Play OP-1 drum kits from a JAMMI slot</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Arpeggiator</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#arp">Arpeggiator for JAMMI samples, synced to the beat</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>USB</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#usb-audio">Audio interface, 4 out, 2 in</a></li>
            <li><a href="#usb-midi">MIDI in and out</a></li>
            <li><a href="#usb-card">Card reader</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block install">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <div>
        <p>Copy the file onto the SD card, remove any other <code>.bin</code> and power on. The LEDs show a slow rainbow while it installs.</p>
        <p>To go back, do the same with <code>CHOMPI_TAPEv2_0.bin</code>.</p>
        <p>Samples and settings live in <code>/MIXTAPE</code>, else <code>/TAPE</code>, else the card root.</p>
        <p>CHOMPI plays from power-on while it reads the card. Pull the card while playing and the sample in memory and the loop play on; put one back and CHOMPI reads it again.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="with-nav">
    <nav class="side" aria-label="Features">
      {nav.map(({ title, id, cards }) => (
        <div>
          <a class="side-head" href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a>
          <ul>{cards.map((card) => <li><a href={`#${card.id}`}>{card.title}</a></li>)}</ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </nav>
    <div class="sections">
    {groups.map(({ title, cards }) => (
      <section class="usage" aria-labelledby={`${title}-head`}>
        <h2 id={`${title}-head`}>{title}</h2>
        <div class="feats">
          {cards.map((card) => <UsageCard {...card} />)}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <section class="usage" aria-labelledby="arp-head">
      <h2 id="arp-head">Arpeggiator</h2>
      <div class="lead" style="--c: var(--green)">
        <figure class="fig"><Panel hl={['knob0']} labels={{ knob0: ['click', 0, -90] }} /></figure>
        <figure class="fig"><Diagram type="flow" steps={[['PITCH'], ['GAIN'], ['ARP', LED.green]]} back /></figure>
        <p>Click the left knob twice to reach the arp page.<br>The arp is only available for JAMMI samples.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feats">
        {arp.map((card) => <UsageCard {...card} />)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="usage" aria-labelledby="usb-head">
      <h2 id="usb-head">USB</h2>
      <div class="lead" style="--c: var(--blue)">
        <p>Connect CHOMPI to a computer with a USB cable. It appears as an audio interface and a MIDI device, and can hand over its SD card as a drive. A serial port named “CHOMPI log” reports errors for troubleshooting; you can ignore it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feats">
        {usb.map((card) => <UsageCard {...card} />)}
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>
    </div>

    <footer>Not an official CHOMPI Club release. CHOMPI is a trademark of CHOMPI Club.</footer>
  </main>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/masonry.js';
  </script>
</body>
</html>
